  "notes": [
    "Retained initial HPOWERNOTIFY integer/null and unsafe native-fixture call diagnostics. Corrected types/safety boundaries; no lint exclusions.",
    "Nullable power percentages exposed a broad bubble percent guard. Narrow it to actual download/tool events, matching native rendering; never replace unknown battery with a fake0/100 percentage.",
    "Initial frontend typecheck failure and intermediate logs remain. Final npm verify and separate automation lint are green.",
    "Power changes now expire4s from creation even while hidden/queued/disabled; duplicates never reset/revive them. This deliberately replaces the previous permanent charging/low fixture behavior, and the existing cleanup test now uses explicit PowerRemoved.",
    "The first native Peek locator matched both the outgoing compact layer and the new details region during a normal crossfade. Scope the selector to the semantic Battery status region; keep failed reports/three pre-Peek captures. No production source or policy change.",
    "Final release is built after the final frontend and verifies embedded JS/all static styles. Native acceptance uses the normal4s policy and only an injected held cursor/reduced-motion fact for stable Peek capture; no OS settings/cursor change.",
    "Previous v51-v55 evidence is unchanged. No actual AC/battery/sleep change, user profile/account, hosted Tack, real clipboard/global input, OS setting, installer or signing is used. Real notification registration/unregistration is tested against a disposable hidden HWND."
